    {
      "id": 15,
      "text": "The 30° line through the shoulder meets the horizontal at the outer end of a small kite. Copy it round.",
      "create": {
        "L4_0": {"line": {"through": "V3", "parallelTo": "h"}},
        "L4_30": {"line": {"through": "V5", "parallelTo": "r30"}},
        "V4": {"point": {"meet": ["L4_0", "L4_30"]}},
        "V4s": {"repeat": {"of": ["V4"], "by": "rot12"}}
      },
      "animate": "ruler"
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "text": "Through the inner end of a petal draw a line at 45°: it meets the horizontal at the tip of the small black kite between two petals. Copy it round. The twelve tips and twelve petal ends make the star at the centre.",
      "create": {
        "L0_45": {"line": {"through": "V2", "parallelTo": "r45"}},
        "V0": {"point": {"meet": ["L0_45", "h"]}},
        "V0s": {"repeat": {"of": ["V0"], "by": "rot12"}}
      },
      "animate": "ruler"
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "text": "Open the compass from A to the point between two petals at 60°, and draw that circle about O. Where it crosses the horizontal, draw a line at right angles: one side of the twelve-sided rim around the rosette. Copy it round.",
      "create": {
        "cr": {"circle": {"centre": "O", "radiusFrom": ["A", "V3@2"]}},
        "RA": {"point": {"meet": ["cr", "h"], "pick": {"angle": 0.0}}},
        "rim": {"line": {"through": "RA", "perpendicularTo": "h"}},
        "rims": {"repeat": {"of": ["rim"], "by": "rot12"}}
      },
      "highlight": ["A", "V3@2"],
      "animate": "compass"
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "text": "Mark the corners of the rim at 15° and 45°, and draw the level line through the 45° corner.",
      "create": {
        "R15": {"point": {"meet": ["rim", "rim@1"]}},
        "R45": {"point": {"meet": ["rim@1", "rim@2"]}},
        "oh": {"line": {"through": "R45", "parallelTo": "h"}}
      },
      "highlight": ["rim", "rim@1"],
      "animate": "ruler"
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "text": "Through K draw the other diagonal. The eight-pointed star at K is two squares: one square’s sides are the rims of the four rosettes around it; the other, turned square has its sides as far from K. Set the compass to that distance (from the rim side to A), draw it about K, and draw the turned square’s sides across the diagonals where the circle cuts them.",
      "create": {
        "ad": {"line": {"through": "K", "perpendicularTo": "r45"}},
        "cs": {"circle": {"centre": "K", "radiusFrom": ["RA", "A"]}},
        "Sr450": {"point": {"meet": ["cs", "r45"], "pick": {"nearest": "O"}}},
        "SLr450": {"line": {"through": "Sr450", "perpendicularTo": "r45"}},
        "Sr451": {"point": {"meet": ["cs", "r45"], "pick": {"farthest": "O"}}},
        "SLr451": {"line": {"through": "Sr451", "perpendicularTo": "r45"}},
        "Sad0": {"point": {"meet": ["cs", "ad"], "pick": {"angle": 49.222}}},
        "SLad0": {"line": {"through": "Sad0", "perpendicularTo": "ad"}},
        "Sad1": {"point": {"meet": ["cs", "ad"], "pick": {"angle": 40.778}}},
        "SLad1": {"line": {"through": "Sad1", "perpendicularTo": "ad"}}
      },
      "highlight": ["K", "RA", "A"],
      "animate": "compass"
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "text": "The ring around the star is two octagons. The inner one has its square sides through the rim’s 45° corner, the outer one its diagonal side: draw a circle about K through each, and the octagon sides across the grid lines and the diagonals where the circles cut them.",
